%% caption: A transaction, end to end
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant C as Client
    participant G as GRV proxy
    participant P as Commit proxy
    participant R as Resolver
    participant T as Transaction logs
    participant S as Storage servers
    C->>G: get a read version
    G-->>C: version N
    C->>S: reads at version N — consistent snapshot
    C->>P: commit with read and write conflict ranges
    P->>R: does anything conflict since version N?
    alt conflict
        R-->>C: retry — optimistic concurrency, no locks were ever held
    else clean
        R->>T: assign a commit version, make it durable
        T->>S: apply asynchronously
        P-->>C: committed
    end
    Note over C,S: five-second transaction limit — long scans must be chunked
